The PC-FX's and the Virtual Boy's saves stay in memory too.

Patch 0007 did this for the Saturn. The PC-FX writes its backup memory to
a file two seconds after a game changes it, and the Virtual Boy writes a
cartridge's memory when the game is closed. In Chimera a save is part of
the machine's memory, where a savestate holds it, and the user writes it
to a file with Export Save Data.

So the PC-FX's two save functions and the Virtual Boy's write do nothing,
and both systems say where their save memories are
(MDFN_ChimeraSaveMemory): the PC-FX's own backup memory ("sav", 32 KB) and
its memory pack's ("fxb", 128 KB), and a Virtual Boy cartridge's ("sav",
64 KB). Loading is untouched.

--- a/src/pcfx/pcfx.cpp
+++ b/src/pcfx/pcfx.cpp
@@ -780,6 +780,15 @@
 
  MDFN_BackupSavFile(10, "sav");
  MDFN_BackupSavFile(10, "fxb");
+#if defined(CHIMERA_CORE)
+ // chimera: the memories that outlive the power switch, for Export Save Data:
+ // the console's own backup memory and the memory pack's
+ if(!BRAMDisabled)
+ {
+  MDFN_ChimeraSaveMemory("sav", BackupRAM, 0x8000, false);
+  MDFN_ChimeraSaveMemory("fxb", ExBackupRAM, 0x20000, false);
+ }
+#endif
 
  // Default to 16-bit bus.
  for(int i = 0; i < 256; i++)
@@ -979,6 +988,11 @@
 
